James Rising received an email from Omid Tarashtwal, a first-generation student from Afghanistan, expressing his interest in pursuing a PhD under his supervision. Omid detailed his background, including his education in development economics and agricultural economics, and how it aligns with James’s research on climate change and food systems. James requested a professional, succinct response that communicated he would not be taking new PhD students this year. In the drafted response, he acknowledged Omid's impressive journey and encouraged him to pursue his goals in sustainable development while wishing him the best for his future endeavors and PhD applications.
